---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const theorems = (await getCollection('theorems', ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---

<Base title="Linking Proofs of Brouwer, Borsuk–Ulam, and Poincaré" header={false}>
  <main class="home">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Linking Proofs of Brouwer, Borsuk–Ulam, and Poincaré</h1>
      {/* Author list TBD — restore when finalized. */}
      {/* <p class="byline">Thomas F. Banchoff and Dan Margalit</p> */}
      <p class="lede">
        Three famous theorems of topology — Brouwer's fixed point theorem, the
        Borsuk–Ulam theorem, and Poincaré's theorem on vector fields — say
        that certain coincidences are unavoidable. All three of these can be
        proven by a visual, topological technique: slice the domain into circles, graph the resulting functions
        in the solid torus, and appeal to our intuition about knots and links
        in 3-space. Each page below explains one theorem and lets you play
        with an interactive version of its proof.
      </p>
      <p class="paper-link">
        <!-- TODO: replace with the real link when the paper is up. -->
        Read the paper (coming soon)
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <ul class="card-grid">
        {
          theorems.map((t) => (
            <li class="theorem-card">
              <a href={`/${t.id}/`}>
                <h3>{t.data.title}</h3>
                <p>{t.data.blurb}</p>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
